-      TASK:
-      Create a frozen proposal corpus on the 32 audited headline instances using Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, Gemma-4-31B, and Gemma-4-26B-A4B. Retain raw responses, untrusted rationales, parsed action proposals, exact post-generation evaluations, and authentic CUDA receipts for every model-instance unit.
-
-      CONCRETE STEPS:
-      0. PRECONDITIONS: verify the planning_fixture_audit_passed gate; resolve all model files from local cache; verify GGUF magic, hashes, embedded tokenizers, CUDA visibility, VRAM, RAM, disk, owner-bound leases, ports, and no conflicting process. If any mandated model cannot run on CUDA, write a blocked artifact and stop.
-      1. Add or update REQ-* and SCENARIO-* anchors for the frozen proposal corpus. Write focused tests first.
-      2. Define MODEL_SPECS with unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF, unsloth/gemma-4-31B-it-GGUF, and unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF. Resolve with cached_sota_pair() and resolve_cached_gguf(). Legacy small models may run CPU smoke tests only and cannot satisfy a headline row.
-      3. Freeze instance order, model order, prompts, system text, generation settings, seeds, one-call budget, response budget, parser, maximum four extracted proposals, stopping rules, missing-row policy, and exact-evaluation timing before inference.
-      4. Launch fresh owner-bound llama.cpp CUDA processes. Run exactly one planned call per model-instance unit. Ask for candidate action sequences and optional reasoning, but do not expose solver fields, optimum values, labels, or answer-encoding grammar.
-      5. Retain the unmodified response. Extract at most four action sequences without regeneration. Mark parse failures and empty proposal sets; do not silently retry, repair, or substitute a solver plan.
-      6. Only after response commitment, evaluate each proposal with the sealed exact API. Record validity, cost, normalized regret, first failing step, candidate diversity, oracle-at-K headroom, no-headroom, tokens, latency, process identity, and accelerator evidence.
-      7. Report overall and per-model parse yield, proposal count, exact validity, regret, headroom, diversity, cost, missing units, and intervals. Keep model comparisons paired by instance.
-      8. Set proposal_corpus_ready=true only when every planned unit is present or explicitly missing with cause, raw responses and process receipts exist, exact access occurred after commitment, and aggregates recompute from rows.
-      9. Write atomically. Cleanly unload servers and release leases. Run focused tests, scoped coverage, spec coverage, row/artifact/adversarial checks, applicable E2E checks, and git status.
